notes = "[1] This only checks that the folders exist in the correct location.|[2] The core does not require a specific BIOS filename, so this info file|[^] cannot tell you whether the content of your 'bios' folder is correct.|[3] The 'resources' folder must be copied from a matching ARMSX2/PCSX2 build;|[^] the core will not boot without it.|[4] The core shares the frontend's hardware context through the hardware-render|[^] negotiation interface. Vulkan is preferred; OpenGL ES 3.0+ and OpenGL core|[^] 3.3+ are accepted when Vulkan is unavailable.|[5] RetroAchievements are driven by the frontend: the core publishes PS2 main|[^] RAM and the scratchpad, and does not run an rcheevos client of its own.|[6] The core is built once per kernel page size, because that size is compiled|[^] in: armsx2 for 4K kernels and armsx2_16k for 16K ones (Pixel 8 and up,|[^] Android 15 kernels, Asahi). Load the one matching sysconf(_SC_PAGESIZE);|[^] the other refuses to start rather than mapping memory it cannot address."

description = "A libretro port of ARMSX2, a PlayStation 2 emulator forked from PCSX2 for ARM devices, with native arm64 recompilers and mobile-GPU fixes. The core renders through whichever hardware context the frontend grants it. With Vulkan it takes the VkInstance and VkPhysicalDevice from the context-negotiation interface and hands finished frames back through set_image; failing that it asks for OpenGL ES 3.2/3.1/3.0 on mobile or an OpenGL core context (4.6 down to 3.3) on desktop, so a device whose Vulkan driver is missing or unusable still renders. A hardware context of some kind is required -- with none, the core falls back to a null renderer and draws nothing. Place a PS2 BIOS dump in 'system/pcsx2/bios' and a copy of the emulator's 'resources' directory in 'system/pcsx2/resources'. Save states, .m3u disc swapping and the usual renderer/upscale/speedhack core options are implemented. RetroAchievements work with any frontend that runs its own rcheevos client: the core declares achievement support and publishes the PS2's main RAM and scratchpad through both retro_get_memory_data and a libretro memory map. This core is experimental."
